`deno fmt` breaks the call across lines _because_ it is too wide, and a broken object literal gets a
trailing comma. The generator emits the same call on one line with no trailing comma. So the two
writers disagree about punctuation, and fmt can never be idempotent against a build: whichever side
wins, the other rewrites it. No behavioural difference — a trailing comma in an object literal
changes nothing at runtime — but "whitespace-only" would send the next session looking for a
line-width knob when the real fix is a trailing comma the generator has to emit.

## Two trees, one component set — which copy is canonical (design steer #2, pass 8)

**Found 2026-09-04 13:38 UTC.** Design steer #2 was worked in parallel in two worktrees of this same
repo, and both now contain the five widget components:

| Branch                    | Worktree                                              | vs `master` at the time |
| :------------------------ | :---------------------------------------------------- | :---------------------- |
| `design/ledgerline-ui`    | `/home/agent/projects/netscript/wave7-design`         | 9 ahead, **41 behind**  |
| `fix/steer2-consolidated` | `/home/agent/projects/netscript/wave7-billing-steer2` | 25 ahead, **2 behind**  |

`design/ledgerline-ui` branched from `a110230` ("Frontend 1/8: Ledgerline token identity"), before
41 commits of backend work landed on master. `fix/steer2-consolidated` branched from `38f4aee`
("Backend D: terminal compensation proved") and has kept up. Merging the design tree first would
drag that 41-commit divergence along with it, so **`fix/steer2-consolidated` is the canonical line**
and pass 8 worked there. The design tree is not deleted; it is the source of one API worth salvaging
(below).

Consequences for the next session:

- Do not build in `wave7-design` expecting it to converge. Its `SegmentedControl` lacks the `--wrap`
  modifier the runs status filter needs (nine cells overflow a narrow card), so it is the weaker
  copy of that component.
- Do not assume a component exists "because a pass closed it" — check which tree that pass was in.
  Pass 7 ran in the design tree and its two real fixes (chart hover bands, null footer tone) were
  **not** present here; pass 8 ported and verified both (`b0b8612`, `fcc88e3`).
- `MoneyText` still has two shapes. Here it is `components/product/money-text.tsx` with
  `{ value, currency, class }` and hero typography owned by `.ns-widget__hero .ns-money-text`. In
  the design tree it is `components/ui/money-text.tsx` and carries `size`/`signed`/`tone`/`compact`.
  When the trees converge, the card-owns-typography shape is the one to keep — a component that sets
  its own size cannot be re-scaled by the band it sits in — and `signed`/`tone`/`compact` are the
  parts worth porting onto it.

## Dead API — `WidgetCard.Hero`'s `size` prop could not change the size

**Found 2026-09-04 (design steer #2, pass 8).** `WidgetCard.Hero` accepted `size?: 'md' | 'lg'`, and
`--lg`'s rule set `font-size: var(--ns-text-4xl)` — the same value the base
`.ns-widget__hero .ns-money-text` rule already sets. No call site ever passed it. `--ns-text-4xl`
(2.25rem) is the largest type token in `tokens.css`, so there was no step for `lg` to step to; its
only distinct effect was a `padding-block-start`.
